[BEGIN]: The facility monitoring system handles failures through a robust, multi-layered approach. It continuously aggregates sensor data across thermal, acoustic, and vibration channels, correlating anomalies to identify persistent deviations. To avoid false alarms, it applies threshold logic with hysteresis to suppress transient noise. Persistent deviations are automatically escalated to the on-call responder for immediate action. Every decision is logged in an append-only audit trail for accountability and incident analysis. Additionally, the system reconciles clock drift between edge devices to maintain consistent event ordering—critical for accurate incident reconstruction and postmortem analysis. This comprehensive failure handling ensures reliable, traceable, and time-accurate responses across distributed nodes.[END]
